"The prognosis is influenced by several factors, including a preoperative PSA of 16.5 and an ISUP grade group 3 Gleason 4+3 identified both preoperatively and at biopsy. Contributing to risk are positive surgical margins (pT3a) and the absence of documented lymph node metastasis status from sampling. Countervailing findings include no extraprostatic extension, no seminal vesicle invasion, and absent lymphovascular invasion. The biopsy-to-prostatectomy comparison shows concordance in Gleason grade group 3. Missing postoperative PSA data prevents assessment of post-surgical biochemical recurrence trends. Future prognosis revision would depend significantly on the trajectory of any subsequent postoperative PSA measurements. The fixed estimated horizon is 51.41 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 38.56–64.26 months; its coverage has not been validated."
